        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0e994f553c284b39ad581398cbd89067",
      "statement": "The cross-domain change ordering rule is: when a change touches more than one domain, update the shared protocol or the ADR first, then the WebSocket relay/server, then the MCP surface and the shared controller, then the Chrome and Safari browser adapters, then the integration tests, so the explicit contract moves first and the adapters follow. AGENTS.md additionally assigns ownership: shared protocol in packages/shared, relay auth/presence/routing in servers/websocket, agent-facing tools/resources/skills in servers/mcp, and browser-specific integration in clients/extensions/chrome and clients/extensions/safari with adapters kept thin.",
      "evidence": [
