    {
      "id": "claim_be04ef4914c04b89a7e860e7822f2726",
      "statement": "Security docs (THREAT_MODEL.md, TRUST_BOUNDARIES.md, SECURITY_GUARANTEES.md) define the trust boundaries and threat actors that shape the product, encoding mitigations such as explicit request/response, no continuous streaming, user-controlled connections, progressive disclosure, least-privilege permissions, and content that is read rather than evaluated; credential export, session cloning, browser mirroring, ambient surveillance, and MFA interception are deliberate boundaries rather than missing features.",
